{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>Tell me now your name.</b> Since Jacob himself knows that the angel has no fixed name, and he asked the angel his name, he explained that his question concerning his name was only for that moment — and this is the meaning of his saying <b>tell me now your name</b>: meaning, what is your name now." "<b>Why do you ask, etc.</b> The explanation is: granted, the angel's asking Jacob's name serves the purpose of what he told him — ״לֹא יַעֲקֹב וְגוֹ׳ כִּי אִם יִשְׂרָאֵל״ — whereas this question of Jacob's, why? If to tell him something, let him say it to him without the pretext of asking this matter. Or it may intend <b>why</b> to mean: for what purpose do you ask this thing, that I should inform you of my name by which I am called now, since this is not a fixed name and at another time you would need to ask for my name again."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:42.107222544Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}